A fine plan, though even "blessed +4" is likely sufficient.

> 4. Last Wishes in order of priority:
>= of Conflict.

Worth a wish.

> +2 =of Increase Damage

In my opinion, not worth a wish. You'll want to wear conflict and
free action most of the time, and then levitation and one of those two
(depends on taste; I prefer conflict) the rest of the time. The only
places you don't need conflict are the places without swarms of monsters,
and then the increased damage won't do you much good. You might be able
to eat it and get intrinsic damage, but the chances are small enough that
it's better to just save the wish and use it for an emergency cockatrice
corpse down the road. Now _that_ will do some damage. ;)

> And finally... my questions.
>
> What should I expect on the ascention run?

Large swarms of monsters. Unreasonably powerful air elementals.

> Anything else I can to to prepare myself?

Get your HP up. Try the run in Wizmode. Watch some ttyrecs.
Marvin is always good, of course; there's a good rast ttyrec at
yiff.mit.edu/nethackclass/planes_in_140.ttyrec as well. He uses a weird
character set, but Eidolos has cleaned this copy up, so it should display
fine. 

> Any other gear that I need?

Potions of full healing in case you take a lot of damage. Blessed unicorn
horn. A wand of digging or three for Earth.

Best of luck!

